WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.160
Looks like the Batman may have a whole lot
of villainous trouble to deal with when the

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.290
Dark Knight returns.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.559
A fresh report from We Got This Covered has
suggested that Robert Pattinson's version

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:14.330
of the Caped Crusader will face no fewer than
six villains in his first solo outing: the

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.520
Penguin, the Riddler, Catwoman, Two-Face,
Firefly, and the Mad Hatter.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.520
In its coverage of The Batman, the outlet
has previously reported that The Riddler,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.940
the Penguin, Catwoman, Two-Face, Scarecrow
and Bane have all been under consideration

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.340
for a part in the movie's story, with potentially
all six of them showing up at the same time.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.670
According to the more recent report, however,
those last two have been subbed out in favor

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.220
of some slightly more obscure characters.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.160
Before we go on, though, let's note that a
lot can change behind the scenes during the

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.260
development of a movie - especially this particular
movie.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.840
Nothing is certain 'til it's certain - and
any rumors swirling around this project ought

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.160
to be taken with a bunch of grains of you-know-what.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.480
"Could you pass the salt?"

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.560
Of the two new additions to the movie's potential
rogues' gallery, Firefly seems like the best

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:07.079
fit for the noir-styled narrative that writer/director
Matt Reeves reportedly has in mind for the

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.580
film.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.159
The character first appeared way back in 1952,
in Detective Comics #184.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:17.590
An expert in pyrotechnics who plied his trade
in the motion picture industry, Garfield Lynns

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.300
found himself mired in poverty when work dried
up.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:25.360
Like so many of Gotham's destitute citizens,
he soon turned to a life of crime - drawing

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.940
the attention of Batman and Robin, who captured
him during a robbery attempt.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:34.130
In later stories, Lynns enacted his revenge
by lashing out with acts of arson - and soon

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:35.200
took quite a liking to it.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.840
Always on the hunt for bigger and bigger targets,
he eventually set fire to a chemical factory

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.680
and succumbed to the flames himself.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.460
He survived the blaze but was left covered
in severe burns.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.820
Inexplicably, Lynns continued on with his
new line of work, making himself a special

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.719
fire-resistant suit and an array of new weapons
before taking on the guise of the supervillain

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.220
Firefly.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.560
According to We Got This Covered's report,
an early production document indicates that

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.979
Lynn's backstory will possibly be revised
to make him a man in his twenties who grew

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:08.929
up orphaned before embarking on a fiery rampage
against the privileged people of Gotham, which

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:12.420
could make for an interesting parallel with
Batman's own backstory.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.340
The Mad Hatter's history stretches even further
back in DC lore, all the way to his first

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.160
appearance in 1948's Batman #49.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.540
First portrayed as a common criminal with
an unusual affinity for his namesake, Jervis

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.520
Tetch has since been shown to possess a high
degree of skill in electrical engineering,

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.680
which he uses to produce his signature devices:
mind-controlling hats.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.920
As for the other bad guys said to be on tap
for The Batman, any of them could be solid

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.300
choices, just so long as they're done properly.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.629
The Penguin and the Riddler are two iconic
villains whose previous big-screen appearances

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:47.850
tended toward the garish and comedic, and
while Two-Face was certainly done justice

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.680
by Aaron Eckhart's performance in The Dark
Knight, many fans felt that the character

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.300
was given too little screen time.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.200
As for Catwoman - well, whoever ends up taking
that role has some mighty boots to fill.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.530
However it all shakes out, it's important
to remember that none of this is confirmed,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:07.040
and these characters could easily be swapped
out or cut altogether before The Batman's

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.920
final shooting script is in place.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:13.580
After all, front-loading a film with six villains
seems mightily ambitious, and it's not like

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.260
superhero movies haven't struggled to juggle
bad guys in the past.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.760
"Where do all these guys come from?"

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.900
Whatever course Reeves does choose to take,
fans will just have to have faith in his talent

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:35.049
- and hope that the director can deliver both
the Batman we need… and the Batman we deserve.

